Note: a small library: kinds, sorting by a field, filters and lists built from lists.

a book has a title, an author, a year and a rating.

set books to an empty list.
add a new book with title "Dune", author "Frank Herbert", year 1965 and rating 4.5 to books.
add a new book with title "Emma", author "Jane Austen", year 1815 and rating 4.0 to books.
add a new book with title "Solaris", author "Stanislaw Lem", year 1961 and rating 4.2 to books.
add a new book with title "Beloved", author "Toni Morrison", year 1987 and rating 4.4 to books.

to describe a book
  say the title of the book and then "by" and then the author of the book
    and then "(" and then the year of the book and then "), rated" and then the rating of the book.
that's all.

say "By year:".
sort books by year.
for every book in books, describe book.

say "Best rated:" and then the title of (the book in books with the highest rating).
say "Oldest:" and then the title of (the book in books with the smallest year).

set modern to every book in books where the year of book is more than 1950.
say "After 1950:" and then the title of book for every book in modern.
say "Average rating:" and then the average of (the rating of book for every book in books).

sort books by the length of the title of each from highest to lowest.
say "Longest titles first:" and then the title of book for every book in books.
